.TH H96-KERNEL-SWITCH 8 "2026-10-18" "h96-kernel-switch" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
h96-kernel-switch \- boot staged kernel as guarded trial, confirm or roll back
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B h96-kernel-switch
.B list
|
.B status
.br
.B h96-kernel-switch try
.I KREL
.RB [ \-\-auto\-confirm ]
.RB [ \-\-keep\-dtb ]
.br
.B h96-kernel-switch
.B confirm
|
.B rollback
|
.B prune
.I KREL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kernel packages stage files under /usr/lib/h96-kernel/KREL and never write /boot.
Vendor U-Boot on H96 MAX V58 has no try-once slot; boot.scr loads /boot/Image,
/boot/uInitrd and /boot/dtb/FDTFILE.
.B h96-kernel-switch
copies one staged kernel into /boot under versioned names and moves
Image and uInitrd links to it. Boot guard runs early on next boot: on trial
kernel it points links back to previous set at once, so hang, panic or
watchdog reset lands on previous kernel. Only
.B confirm
during trial boot keeps new kernel as default.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Staged kernels with flags running, default, in-boot, trial.
.TP
.B status
Link targets, recorded trial, last results.
.TP
.BI try " KREL"
Checks staged sha256 sums and modules.dep, builds initramfs with mkinitramfs
and mkimage outside /boot, checks free space on /boot (files plus 16 MiB
reserve), copies Image-KREL, uInitrd-KREL and, when board DTB differs,
FDTFILE-KREL, enables guard units, switches links. Previous files stay.
Refuses when trial is recorded, when KREL is running or default, when /boot is
read-only, when extlinux directory exists, or when Image or uInitrd is not link.
.B \-\-auto\-confirm
confirms trial 180 s after boot when multi-user.target is active.
.B \-\-keep\-dtb
leaves board DTB as is.
.TP
.B confirm
Run during trial boot: points links at trial kernel for good.
.TP
.B rollback
With trial recorded: cancels it and points links at previous set. Without
trial: returns links to set that was default before last confirm; running it
again returns to confirmed set.
.TP
.BI prune " KREL"
Removes versioned files of KREL from /boot unless links or records name them.
.SH FILES
.TP
/var/lib/h96-kernel-switch/trial
Recorded trial: phase, previous and new link targets.
.TP
/var/lib/h96-kernel-switch/last
Sets of last confirm, used by rollback.
.TP
/var/lib/h96-kernel-switch/log, result
Action log and outcome lines.
.SH LIMITS
Failure before boot guard runs (early panic, initramfs failure without reset
to userspace) repeats trial boot, since links still name trial kernel at that
point. Recovery then needs rescue media or reflash.
Power loss between two link renames leaves mixed set for one boot; guard reverts
it on next boot that reaches userspace.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkinitramfs (8),
.BR mkimage (1)
